file.content:
[
  {
    "id": "c001",
    "name": "Preamble",
    "text": "This Master Agreement (\"Agreement\") is effective as of ____________, between Axia NGNetworks USA, Inc., a Delaware company registered in Massachusetts and wholly-owned subsidiary of Axia NetMedia Corporation (“Network Operator”) and Massachusetts Technology Park Corporation, an independent public instrumentality of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, established, organized, and existing pursuant to Chapter 40J of the Massachusetts General Laws and doing business as the Massachusetts Technology Collaborative, together with its successors and assigns, (“MTC”)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "1.1.1 Purpose of Agreement",
    "text": "ARTICLE 1. PURPOSE OF AGREEMENT 1.1 Purpose of Agreement 1.1.1 MTC is building the MassBroadband 123 Network, defined herein as the MTC Network, a broadband network currently planned to have fiber in approximately 124 communities in western and north central Massachusetts and initially connect approximately 1,392 community anchor institutions that serve them, all as more fully defined herein."
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "1.1.2 Network Operator experience",
    "text": "1.1.2 Network Operator is a provider of network operations and support services and solutions and is experienced and skilled in the administration, management, maintenance, provisioning, performance and sale of third party access to complex network systems such as the MTC Network."
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "1.1.3 Intended services",
    "text": "1.1.3 MTC is in need of a provider of network operation and support services, as more specifically defined herein, and Network Operator desires to provide such services to MTC, which will include, among other things, providing advice and recommendations to MTC regarding the selection of the appropriate network design, #10069598_v13 1 fiber, equipment, and configuration; participating in acceptance testing of the MTC Network; operating and managing the MTC Network; facilitating the Interconnection of and service to Wholesale Customers; constructing and administering procedures for others to construct Network Extensions on the MTC Network; and upgrading and updating the MTC Network electronics and other equipment to keep the MTC Network operating efficiently and accommodating increasing bandwidth demands."
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "1.1.4 Performance by Network Operator",
    "text": "1.1.4 MTC desires that these services be rendered hereto by Network Operator and that the functions, responsibilities and tasks as described in this Agreement and otherwise commonly performed by a dark fiber and lit network provider be performed and assumed by Network Operator in accordance with this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "Article 2 definition rule",
    "text": "ARTICLE 2. DEFINITIONS In the Agreement all capitalized terms shall have the meanings set forth in this Article 2."
  },
  {
    "id": "c007",
    "name": "2.1 AAA Rules",
    "text": "2.1 AAA Rules shall mean the Commercial Arbitration Rules of the American Arbitration Association in effect at the time a demand for arbitration is made."
  },
  {
    "id": "c008",
    "name": "2.2 Affiliate",
    "text": "2.2 Affiliate shall mean an entity that directly or indirectly controls or is controlled by or is under common control with another entity."
  },
  {
    "id": "c009",
    "name": "2.3 Alterations",
    "text": "2.3 Alterations shall mean alterations, additions and/or modifications to that portion of the MTC Network that is the subject of the MassDOT Operating Agreement and MassDOT Lease Agreement for any purpose consistent with the uses granted in the MassDOT Operating Agreement and MassDOT Lease Agreement, including, without limitation, the installation of additional optical fiber in the initial four empty conduit installed in connection with the project or any thereafter installed empty conduits within the MTC Network covered by these MassDOT agreements, or by connecting a third party’s optical fiber via the shared resources handholes covered by these MassDOT agreements."
  },
  {
    "id": "c010",
    "name": "2.4 Annual Plan",
    "text": "2.4 Annual Plan shall mean the plan submitted annually to MTC pursuant to Section 4.9.2."
  },
  {
    "id": "c011",
    "name": "2.5 Bureau",
    "text": "2.5 Bureau shall mean the United States Bureau of Labor Statistics."
  },
  {
    "id": "c012",
    "name": "2.6 BTOP",
    "text": "2.6 BTOP stands for Broadband Technology Opportunities Program and shall mean the federal program known by that name administered by NTIA."
  },
  {
    "id": "c013",
    "name": "2.7 CAI",
    "text": "2.7 CAI stands for Community Anchor Institution, and shall mean any one of the organizations and agencies identified in Exhibit A hereto, as the same may be revised from time to time in MTC's sole discretion up until the Commencement Date."
  },
  {
    "id": "c014",
    "name": "2.8 Commencement Date",
    "text": "2.8 Commencement Date shall mean the earlier of (a) the date on which MTC has accepted, under the terms of its contract with the Design-Build Contractor, at least ninety percent (90%) of all mileage of the MTC Network the Design-Build Contractor is engaged to construct within the Service Area shown in Exhibit C and ninety percent (90%) of the CAIs have been connected to the MTC Network, or (b) thirty (30) months after the Effective Date."
  },
  {
    "id": "c015",
    "name": "2.9 Confidential Information",
    "text": "2.9 Confidential Information shall mean any information of MTC or the Network Operator that is not generally known to the public and that, at the time of disclosure, is identified, or would reasonably be understood by the Parties, to be proprietary or confidential, whether disclosed in oral, written, visual, electronic or other form, and which a Party (or its contractors or agents) observes or learns in connection with this Agreement. Subject to the requirements of law, including, without limitation, Massachusetts General Laws Chapter 66 and Massachusetts General Laws Chapter 4, Section 7, Clause 26th, Confidential Information may include, but is not necessarily limited to, (a) business plans, strategies, forecasts, projects and analyses, (b), financial information and fee structures, (c) business processes, methods and models, (d) employee information, (e) specifications, (f) manufacturing, purchasing, logistics, #10069598_v13 3 sales, technical, product and marketing information, (g) work product, (h) the existence, terms and conditions of this Agreement, and (i) data in any form, that is collected, copied, processed, transferred or otherwise used by or on behalf of either party in connection with this Agreement, including without limitation, customer information, personal data, trade secrets or corporate proprietary information of any kind whatsoever, which is made available directly or indirectly to the Network Operator in connection with its performance under this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c016",
    "name": "2.10 CPI",
    "text": "2.10 CPI shall mean the Bureau's Consumer Price Index for Urban Wage Earners and Clerical Workers, Boston Metropolitan Area, All Items (1982-84=100)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c017",
    "name": "2.11 Dark Fiber Customer",
    "text": "2.11 Dark Fiber Customer shall mean a lessee of dark fiber on the MTC Network from MTC pursuant to Section 4.7.4."
  },
  {
    "id": "c018",
    "name": "2.12 Design-Build Contractor",
    "text": "2.12 Design-Build Contractor shall mean the entity engaged or to be engaged by MTC to complete the design of and construct the MTC Network."
  },
  {
    "id": "c019",
    "name": "2.13 Dispute Resolution Notice",
    "text": "2.13 Dispute Resolution Notice shall mean a written request of either Party to the other Party intended to initiate resolution of a dispute pursuant to ARTICLE 11."
  },
  {
    "id": "c020",
    "name": "2.14 EOPSS",
    "text": "2.14 EOPSS shall mean the Massachusetts Executive Office of Public Safety and Security or any functional successor within Massachusetts state government."
  },
  {
    "id": "c021",
    "name": "2.15 Effective Date",
    "text": "2.15 Effective Date shall mean the date first stated above."
  },
  {
    "id": "c022",
    "name": "2.16 FCC",
    "text": "2.16 FCC shall mean the Federal Communications Commission."
  },
  {
    "id": "c023",
    "name": "2.17 Fiber Management Plan",
    "text": "2.17 Fiber Management Plan shall mean the Network Operator’s plan required by Section 4.5.2."
  },
  {
    "id": "c024",
    "name": "2.18 Financial Statement",
    "text": "2.18 Financial Statement shall mean any financial statements of Network Operator delivered to MTC or its designee in connection with this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c025",
    "name": "2.19 Force Majeure Event",
    "text": "2.19 Force Majeure Event shall mean an event constituting or arising from any substantial and extraordinary cause beyond a Party's reasonable control, including, without limitation, acts of war, acts of God, earthquake, hurricanes, embargo, riot, sabotage, strikes, governmental act, insurrections, epidemics, quarantines, terrorist activity, extraordinarily severe or prolonged flooding, extraordinarily severe or prolonged ice and snow storms, extraordinarily severe and widespread fire or other similar casualty, or other substantial and extraordinary accidents not caused by the Party asserting such Force Majeure Event, or strikes or utility company delays not resulting from the responsible Party's or such Party’s subcontractor’s failure to timely take necessary actions."
  },
  {
    "id": "c026",
    "name": "2.20 IFRS",
    "text": "2.20 IFRS shall mean International Financial Reporting Standards."
  },
  {
    "id": "c027",
    "name": "2.21 Grant",
    "text": "2.21 Grant shall mean the grant of $45.4 million to MTC, award number NT10BIX5570070, awarded by NTIA on July 1, 2010, as part of BTOP for the construction of the MTC Network."
  },
  {
    "id": "c028",
    "name": "2.22 Indemnified Claim",
    "text": "2.22 Indemnified Claim shall mean a claim by an Indemnified Party for indemnification under the provisions of ARTICLE 9."
  },
  {
    "id": "c029",
    "name": "2.23 Indemnified Claim Proceeding",
    "text": "2.23 Indemnified Claim Proceeding shall mean any mediation, arbitration, legal and/or administrative action or other proceeding regarding an Indemnified Claim."
  },
  {
    "id": "c030",
    "name": "2.24 Indemnified Party",
    "text": "2.24 Indemnified Party shall mean, with respect to a Party, the other Party and its Affiliates, officers, directors, employees, agents, successors and assigns."
  },
  {
    "id": "c031",
    "name": "2.25 Indemnifying Party",
    "text": "2.25 Indemnifying Party shall mean the Party from which another person seeks or is entitled to indemnification hereunder."
  },
  {
    "id": "c032",
    "name": "2.26 Interconnection",
    "text": "2.26 Interconnection shall mean any connection of fiber, either active or passive, to the MTC Network."
  },
  {
    "id": "c033",
    "name": "2.27 IPT",
    "text": "2.27 IPT stands for Integrated Planning Team and shall mean the body established pursuant to ARTICLE 6 of this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c034",
    "name": "2.28 IRU",
    "text": "2.28 IRU stands for and shall mean an Indefeasible Right of Use."
  },
  {
    "id": "c035",
    "name": "2.29 ISP",
    "text": "2.29 ISP stands for and shall mean an Internet service provider."
  },
  {
    "id": "c036",
    "name": "2.30 ITD",
    "text": "2.30 ITD shall mean the Information Technology Division of the Executive Office for Administration and Finance of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts or any functional successor within Massachusetts state government."
  },
  {
    "id": "c037",
    "name": "2.31 KPI",
    "text": "2.31 KPI stands for Key Performance Indicator and shall mean any of the rating factors used to measure the performance of the Network Operator or the MTC Network in critical areas of operation and management."
  },
  {
    "id": "c038",
    "name": "2.32 MassDOT",
    "text": "2.32 MassDOT shall mean the Massachusetts Department of Transportation or any functional successor within Massachusetts state government."
  },
  {
    "id": "c039",
    "name": "2.33 MassDOT Lease Agreement",
    "text": "2.33 MassDOT Lease Agreement shall mean the agreement entered into effective as of January 21, 2011 with MassDOT setting forth the terms of the lease for the 55 miles of facility assets on I-91and approximately 1.5 miles of facility assets on I-291 leased to MTC by MassDOT."
  },
  {
    "id": "c040",
    "name": "2.34 MassDOT Operating Agreement",
    "text": "2.34 MassDOT Operating Agreement shall mean the agreement entered into effective as of January 21, 2011 between MTC and MassDOT setting forth the terms of the operation of the 55 mile I-91 facility assets and approximately 1.5 miles facility assets on I-291 leased to MTC by MassDOT."
  },
  {
    "id": "c041",
    "name": "2.35 MBI",
    "text": "2.35 MBI shall mean the Massachusetts Broadband Institute, a division of MTC or any functional successor within Massachusetts state government."
  },
  {
    "id": "c042",
    "name": "2.36 MBI Network Extension",
    "text": "2.36 MBI Network Extension shall mean a Network Extension constructed or acquired by MTC and funded in whole or in part by MTC. MBI Network Extensions become integral parts of the MTC Network upon completion or acquisition."
  },
  {
    "id": "c043",
    "name": "2.37 MTC",
    "text": "2.37 MTC stands for the Massachusetts Technology Collaborative and means the Massachusetts Technology Park Corporation, 75 North Drive, Westborough, MA 01581, an independent public instrumentality of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts (the “Commonwealth”), established, organized, and existing pursuant to Chapter 40J of the Massachusetts General Laws and doing business as the Massachusetts Technology Collaborative acting in accordance with G. L. c. 40J, § 6B, and is the Party identified as MTC in the first paragraph of this Agreement or any functional successor within Massachusetts state government."
  },
  {
    "id": "c044",
    "name": "2.38 MTC Network",
    "text": "2.38 MTC Network shall mean the network as built or acquired by the MassBroadband 123 Project including any MBI Network Extensions and IRUs. The MTC Network is currently planned as a 1,338-mile fiber-optic network with new fiber running through or near 124 communities in western and north central Massachusetts, including without limitation 55 miles of facility assets on I-91 and approximately 1.5 miles of facility assets on I-291 leased to MTC by MassDOT. At the point of its initial design, the MTC Network is planned to include the fiber backbone, lateral fiber lines and direct connections (including electronics) at approximately 1,392 CAIs, including approximately 23 active POIs and Internet points of presence at One Federal Street, Springfield, MA, and at One Summer Street, Boston, MA."
  },
  {
    "id": "c045",
    "name": "2.39 Network Extension",
    "text": "2.39 Network Extension shall mean any fiber optic cable extension of or from the MTC Network the construction of which costs more than $10,000 in direct trade labor, #10069598_v13 7 materials and equipment, and includes, without limitation, Network Operator Network Extensions and MBI Network Extensions. A fiber optic cable extension of or from the MTC Network shall become part of the MTC Network unless it is a Network Extension and the Network Operator establishes to MTC's reasonable satisfaction that it is not or does not become part of the MTC Network under this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c046",
    "name": "2.40 Network Operator",
    "text": "2.40 Network Operator shall mean the entity identified as such in the first paragraph of this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c047",
    "name": "2.41 Network Operator Dark Fiber Rights",
    "text": "2.41 Network Operator Dark Fiber Rights shall mean rights obtained pursuant to Section 3.6.1 to lease dark fiber on the MTC Network."
  },
  {
    "id": "c048",
    "name": "2.42 Network Operator Network Extension",
    "text": "2.42 Network Operator Network Extension shall mean a Network Extension funded and owned by the Network Operator but excludes any Network Extension funded by MTC unless otherwise agreed."
  },
  {
    "id": "c049",
    "name": "2.43 Network Operator Network Extension Fees",
    "text": "2.43 Network Operator Network Extension Fees shall mean the amount of fees deemed to be incurred by Network Operator to connect Network Operator Network Extensions to the MTC Network and/or to use and maintain such connections to the MTC Network, which deemed fees shall be equal to the amount(s) as would be paid by Third Party Service Providers to Network Operator for similar services on the MTC Network pursuant to the then current Price Schedule, whether one-time fees or recurring fees as provided in the Price Schedule. For avoidance of doubt, by way of example only: if the Price Schedule has a price of $475 per month for Ethernet-100 (100 Mbps uncontended Ethernet service), and Network Operator uses such service on a Network Operator Network Extension via its connection to the MTC Network, then that amount shall be deemed to be Network Operator Network Extension Fees #10069598_v13 8 since a third party would have had to pay that amount to Network Operator had it used that service in that manner."
  },
  {
    "id": "c050",
    "name": "2.44 Network Policies",
    "text": "2.44 Network Policies refers to the set of policies required by the NTIA BTOP Notice of Funding Availability dated January 22, 2010 plus any additional policies reasonably required by MTC to meet legal requirements for operation of the MTC Network. At present this is includes MTC's Open Access Policy, the framework of which is shown in Exhibit G; the FCC's Interconnection Policy; the FCC's Non-Discrimination Policy; the FCC's Choice of Carrier Policy; the FCC’s Broadband Policy Statement (FCC 05-151 adopted Aug. 5, 2005); 220 C.M.R. §§45.00 et seq.; the approved Fiber Management Plan; the approved network management policy, the FHWA Utility Accommodation Policy, as established by the Federal Highway Administration and administered by MassDOT."
  },
  {
    "id": "c051",
    "name": "2.45 Network Revenue",
    "text": "2.45 Network Revenue refers to all revenue recognized by the Network Operator during the initial Term of this Agreement or any subsequent Renewal Terms, calculated on a gross basis, without deductions or allowances, employing IFRS except as otherwise expressly provided in this Agreement, from (a) the sales, provisioning, support, and fees paid for bandwidth and other use of the MTC Network; (b) all Network Operator Network Extension Fees deemed incurred; (c) MTC's Master Services Agreement with EOPSS and ITD; and (d) a lease of dark fiber on the MTC Network, but only that portion of payments received by the Network Operator payable under Section 4.7.4.5 to Network Operator during the Term of this Agreement. Network Revenue shall include the proceeds of any rental loss insurance coverage or equivalent, pursuant to Section 10.2.8. Any amounts earned by Network Operator from services related to the MTC Network, other than the categories expressly excluded in this definition, shall be Network Revenue unless MTC agrees otherwise in writing. Network #10069598_v13 9 Revenue shall not include: revenues earned by a retail Affiliate of the Network Operator or revenues earned by the Network Operator from offering (w) value-added services based on protocols commonly transported over the Internet, (x) professional services unrelated to the MTC Network, (y) co-location at facilities not leased by MTC or (z) services on Network Operator Network Extensions. Network Revenue also shall not include that portion of payments for leases of dark fiber received by the Network Operator payable under Section 4.7.4.5 to MTC during the Term of this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c052",
    "name": "2.46 Network Segment",
    "text": "2.46 Network Segment shall mean any portion of the MTC Network as may be defined (a) by MTC during the design and construction of the MTC Network, and thereafter (b) by mutual agreement of MTC and the Network Operator."
  },
  {
    "id": "c053",
    "name": "2.47 NOC",
    "text": "2.47 NOC stands for Network Operations Center and shall mean a facility established by the Network Operator to be staffed and to provide, at a minimum, monitoring, troubleshooting, customer support, dispatch, and engineering services as required herein."
  },
  {
    "id": "c054",
    "name": "2.48 NTIA",
    "text": "2.48 NTIA shall mean the National Telecommunications and Information Administration within the U.S. Department of Commerce."
  },
  {
    "id": "c055",
    "name": "2.49 Officer's Certificate",
    "text": "2.49 Officer's Certificate shall mean a document signed under the penalties of perjury by an officer of the entity providing the document to another, the contents of which shall be binding upon the entity."
  },
  {
    "id": "c056",
    "name": "2.50 Party",
    "text": "2.50 Party shall mean each of MTC and Network Operator."
  },
  {
    "id": "c057",
    "name": "2.51 POI",
    "text": "2.51 POI stands for Point of Interconnection and shall mean a node that enables the Network Operator or Wholesale Customer to connect to the MTC Network without splicing MTC Network fiber in order to provide services to other customers, including but not limited to consumers, government entities, businesses and non-profit organizations that are not directly #10069598_v13 10 connected to the MTC Network. The MTC Network is currently planned to include 23 new POIs, including the Internet points of presence at 1 Federal Street, Springfield, MA and One Summer Street, Boston, MA."
  },
  {
    "id": "c058",
    "name": "2.52 Price Caps",
    "text": "2.52 Price Caps shall mean the prices set forth in Exhibit F to this Agreement applicable to Wholesale Service provided by the Network Operator as specified herein."
  },
  {
    "id": "c059",
    "name": "2.53 Price Schedule",
    "text": "2.53 Price Schedule shall mean the charges by the Network Operator for Wholesale Service on the MTC Network and shall include prices and terms for all standard offerings, including bandwidth services, interconnection fees, dark fiber leases and services, installation and configuration fees, and consulting rates for custom consulting services related to the Wholesale Services provided herein. Nothing in the published Price Schedule shall prevent the Network Operator from offering, subject to MTC approval, additional custom quotations for non-standard customer requests or for Services not included in the Price Schedule. For avoidance of doubt, the Price Schedule shall not determine prices the Network Operator may charge to customers of Network Operator Network Extensions, which prices are determined by the Network Operator in its sole discretion, except that charges for bandwidth to MassDOT, ITD or EOPSS shall be governed by Section 4.7.2 regardless of whether they are connected on the MTC Network or on a Network Operator Network Extension."
  },
  {
    "id": "c060",
    "name": "2.54 Renewal Decision",
    "text": "2.54 Renewal Decision shall mean a written decision by MTC conforming to the requirements of Section 3.2 and responding to a Renewal Request."
  },
  {
    "id": "c061",
    "name": "2.55 Renewal Request",
    "text": "2.55 Renewal Request shall mean a written request by MTC or the Network Operator to enter into negotiations for a Renewal Term, conforming to the requirements of Section 3.3."
  },
  {
    "id": "c062",
    "name": "2.56 Renewal Term",
    "text": "2.56 Renewal Term shall mean any additional period of years for which the Term of this Agreement is extended pursuant to the terms of this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c063",
    "name": "2.57 Retail Service",
    "text": "2.57 Retail Service shall mean services provided by a Third Party Service Provider."
  },
  {
    "id": "c064",
    "name": "2.58 Scheduled Maintenance",
    "text": "2.58 Scheduled Maintenance shall mean routine scheduled maintenance and repair of the MTC Network as described herein, including in Section 4.11.2."
  },
  {
    "id": "c065",
    "name": "2.59 Service Area",
    "text": "2.59 Service Area shall mean the portion of the MTC Network shown on the Service Area Map attached as Exhibit C."
  },
  {
    "id": "c066",
    "name": "2.60 Services",
    "text": "2.60 Services shall mean all performance obligations of the Network Operator hereunder."
  },
  {
    "id": "c067",
    "name": "2.61 SLA",
    "text": "2.61 SLA stands for Service Level Agreement and shall mean an agreement setting forth and/or identifying the services, priorities, responsibilities, and network management policies controlling the day-to-day operations and servicing standards of the Network Operator. Each area of service is separately defined and specifies the levels of availability, serviceability, performance, operation and other attributes of service on the MTC Network."
  },
  {
    "id": "c068",
    "name": "2.62 Splice",
    "text": "2.62 Splice is a connection of two strands of fiber, at least one of which is part of the MTC Network."
  },
  {
    "id": "c069",
    "name": "2.63 Term",
    "text": "2.63 Term shall mean the period of time from the Effective Date until the expiration or termination of this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c070",
    "name": "2.64 Third Party Service Provider",
    "text": "2.64 Third Party Service Provider shall mean any organization other than Network Operator providing retail broadband service to an end user or reselling wholesale broadband services, and shall include, without limitation, ISPs, fiber companies, cable TV companies, fixed and mobile wireless carriers, competitive local exchange carriers, incumbent local #10069598_v13 12 exchange carriers, and interexchange carriers receiving Wholesale Service from the Network Operator in order to, in turn, deliver services to its customers."
  },
  {
    "id": "c071",
    "name": "2.65 Unscheduled Maintenance",
    "text": "2.65 Unscheduled Maintenance shall mean non-routine maintenance and repair of the MTC Network which is not included in Scheduled Maintenance."
  },
  {
    "id": "c072",
    "name": "2.66 Wholesale Customer",
    "text": "2.66 Wholesale Customer shall mean any customer purchasing Wholesale Services, including a Dark Fiber Customer, a Third Party Service Provider, MassDOT, EOPSS or ITD."
  },
  {
    "id": "c073",
    "name": "2.67 Wholesale Service",
    "text": "2.67 Wholesale Service shall mean (a) any service provided over the MTC Network by the Network Operator to a Third Party Service Provider or to MassDOT, EOPSS or ITD, (b) leasing of dark fiber to persons other than the Network Operator to the extent permitted hereunder, and services required under such leases, and (c) lit transmission service of not less than 10 Gbps to an institutional customer without protocol."
  },
  {
    "id": "c074",
    "name": "3.1 Term",
    "text": "ARTICLE 3. TERM OF AGREEMENT AND RENEWAL 3.1 The Term of this Master Agreement will begin as of the Effective Date and will terminate upon the tenth (10th) anniversary of the Commencement Date, unless earlier terminated, extended or renewed in accordance with the provisions of this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c075",
    "name": "3.2 Renewal Terms",
    "text": "3.2 This Agreement may be renewed by mutual agreement of the parties for two (2) successive Renewal Terms of five (5) years each, subject to the conditions set forth herein and subject to the right of MTC hereunder to terminate this Agreement for cause. The parties may, but are not required to, agree upon options for additional Renewal Terms by an amendment to this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c076",
    "name": "3.3 Renewal Request timing",
    "text": "3.3 Should the Parties elect to renew the Agreement, they will do so in accordance with the following time requirements, with time being of the essence. At any time within the period from thirty (30) to thirty-two (32) months prior to the expiration of the then current Term of the Agreement, MTC or the Network Operator may make a Renewal Request, by #10069598_v13 13 written Notice to the other in conformity with Section 12.12, to extend the Term for a Renewal Term ending five (5) years beyond the then-pending termination date."
  },
  {
    "id": "c077",
    "name": "3.4 Renewal negotiations",
    "text": "3.4 Upon receipt by either Party of such a Renewal Request, the Parties shall, within thirty (30) days thereof, enter into good faith negotiations on the terms of the renewal. Either Party may terminate such negotiations by written notice to the other Party at any time after the date that is twenty-eight (28) months prior to the expiration of the then current Term of the Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c078",
    "name": "3.5 Renewal commencement",
    "text": "3.5 In the event that the Parties agree to a renewal that results in a five (5) year extension of the Agreement, the first such Renewal Term shall begin on the tenth anniversary date of the Commencement Date. Any subsequent Renewal Term agreed upon in accordance with the process set forth in Section 3.2 shall begin five (5) anniversaries after the commencement of the last agreed Renewal Term."
  },
  {
    "id": "c079",
    "name": "3.6.1 Dark Fiber Rights conditions",
    "text": "3.6 Network Operator Dark Fiber Rights Upon Termination or Expiration of the Agreement. 3.6.1 Unless MTC terminates this Agreement for cause, then upon expiration of the Term, subject to (x) obtaining the prior approval of NTIA and any other governmental or regulatory authority having jurisdiction which MTC will use reasonable efforts to obtain and (y) cure, prior to expiration of the Term, of any existing defaults, Network Operator will have the following Network Operator Dark Fiber Rights:"
  },
  {
    "id": "c080",
    "name": "3.6.1.1 Quantity",
