    "name": "4.1 Overview of Network Operator's Responsibilities",
    "text": "ARTICLE 4. NETWORK MANAGEMENT, CUSTOMER SERVICE, MAINTENANCE AND FINANCIAL OBLIGATIONS OF NETWORK OPERATOR 4.1 Overview of Network Operator's Responsibilities. The Network Operator is responsible for all aspects of the management, sales, monitoring, operations, support, and maintenance of the MTC Network. The Network Operator will perform its duties pursuant to this Agreement subject to the reasonable oversight by MTC as set forth herein and MTC's reasonable cooperation with Network Operator in fulfilling the overall objective. In addition to responsibilities set forth in other Sections of this Agreement, Network Operator's responsibilities include, generally: 4.1.1 Managing the physical plant and operations of the MTC Network, including development and publication, subject to MTC's approval, of policies, procedures, systems and controls to ensure the effective operation and optimal use of MTC Network resources, performing all required maintenance and repair, including Dig Safe mark-out on MTC-owned conduit, tree trimming on MTC-owned poles, periodic inspection of facilities, resolving engineering issues, paying all reoccurring maintenance, attachment, and restoration fees of any kind, managing relationships with vendors and service providers, recommending and implementing equipment maintenance strategies and upgrades, tracking customer use of the network for billing and capacity planning purposes; 4.1.2 Maintaining records of all network fiber in the Attachment Database, in accordance with the Fiber Management Plan, which shall include, without limitation, fiber cable route on all Network Extensions, detailed records on splice case configuration, #10069598_v13 22 fiber optic strand continuity and splice map, patch panel configuration, outside plant elements like slack loops, patch panels, cabinets, and splice cases, and attachments; 4.1.3 Maintain, for at least seven (7) years beyond the Term, detailed and accurate records and accounts relating to all payments, transactions and other obligations, responsibilities and rights of the Network Operator under this Agreement; 4.1.4 Make timely payment for all costs for which the Network Operator is responsible under this Agreement; 4.1.5 Monitoring, documenting and reporting on all aspects of the MTC Network including, without limitation, accumulating network performance information to provide information needed to measure performance against KPIs or to detect degradation or network failures of the physical or electronic components; 4.1.6 Maintaining and managing the staff, consultants, agents, and contractors required to support the MTC Network, including human resources functions, development and publication, subject to MTC reasonable approval, of policies and procedures relating thereto, staffing for 24x7 monitoring of the network, and dispatch of field technicians as needed; 4.1.7 All aspects of marketing, sales, contracting, contract management, billing, insurance claims processing, customer support and relations with Wholesale Customers, including, without limitation, leasing of dark fiber (as MTC's agent as specified below), entering into SLAs for lit service, maintenance of websites and development and deployment of customer forms, answering customer inquiries, tracking and resolving customer requests and problems, provisioning services to customers in accordance with their needs and in the timeframes specified in SLAs, performing capacity planning, #10069598_v13 23 detecting and resolving performance degradations, and providing necessary information to MTC and customers; 4.1.8 As MTC’s agent, managing relations with third party facility owners that grant or have granted MTC attachment rights. The Network Operator shall be administratively responsible for ensuring compliance with all of the requirements of such attachment agreements obtained for the MTC Network. These responsibilities shall include, without limitation, timely responding to facility owner and third party requests for make-ready, facility moves and changes, complying with requirements to use and update third party pole life cycle management systems, subscribing to pole owners' pole lifecycle management systems and double pole notification systems and coordinating with other attachers; and 4.1.9 As MTC's agent, managing and ensuring compliance with the Network Policies, attachment agreements and other third party contracts, and applicable federal, state and local law, and taking the initiative to plan and manage, subject to MTC approval, MTC Network stakeholder engagement and communication. The Network Operator shall be administratively responsible for ensuring compliance with all of the requirements of such agreements, contracts and laws."
