  "id": "c117",
  "name": "4.5.7 MBI Network Extensions",
  "text": "4.5.7 MBI Network Extensions. Following consultation and coordination with the Network Operator, MTC may elect to develop MBI Network Extensions. The construction and operation of any MBI Network Extensions may be performed by an entity selected by MTC independent of this Agreement. Network Operator shall have the same role and rights relative to the MBI Network Extensions as are set forth in section 4.2 of this Agreement or as otherwise agreed between MTC and Network Operator, and any such MBI Network Extension shall be designed, constructed and operated in a manner consistent with, and that will not adversely affect achievement by Network Operator of, the obligations under any SLA with respect to the MTC Network. MTC shall own any MBI Network Extension, regardless of the source of its funding, which shall become part of the MTC Network and Network Operator shall maintain and operate it as such."
},
{
  "id": "c118",
  "name": "4.6.1 System Upgrades and Updates",
  "text": "4.6 System Upgrades and Updates 4.6.1 Network Operator is required to periodically update or upgrade the electronics and other components on the MTC Network during the Term of this Agreement in order to maintain the carrier-grade quality and reliability of services offered thereon. Upgrades to the capacity and performance of the MTC Network are to #10069598_v13 34 be made in order to support customer needs or provide new and enhanced services over the MTC Network. Updates and upgrades of the fiber and other components of the MTC Network will be funded through the CAPEX Upgrade and Update Fund as provided in Section 4.9.6, below. Network Operator may undertake such expenditures as may be available in the CAPEX Upgrade and Update Fund for upgrading and updating the MTC Network subject to the then-current Annual Plan approved by MTC. Additionally, MTC may reasonably direct Network Operator to undertake capital expenditures required to upgrade or update the MTC Network, provided that these expenditures will not exceed the currently available amount in the CAPEX Upgrade and Update Fund."
},
{
  "id": "c119",
  "name": "4.6.2 Additional resources",
  "text": "4.6.2 Nothing in this Section precludes MTC or the Network Operator from using its own resources, in excess of the CAPEX Upgrade and Update Fund, to make upgrades or updates to the MTC Network."
},
{
  "id": "c120",
  "name": "4.7.1 Wholesale Service responsibility",
  "text": "4.7 Wholesale Service 4.7.1 Network Operator is solely and fully responsible for the marketing, provisioning and support of such Wholesale Service to Wholesale Customers as may be required by these providers to, in turn, deliver services to end users. Any and all functions, responsibilities, activities and tasks, whether or not specifically described in this Agreement or in Wholesale Customer contracts, which are required for the proper performance and provision of the Services are an inherent part of, or a necessary sub-part included within, the Services. If such functions, responsibilities, activities and tasks are determined to be required for the proper performance and provision of the Services or are an inherent part, or a necessary sub-part included within, the Services, such functions, responsibilities, activities and tasks shall be deemed to be implied by and included within #10069598_v13 35 the scope of the Services, to the same extent and in the same manner as if specifically described in the Agreement (and, as applicable, Wholesale Customer contracts). Each such determination shall be made by agreement of the Parties or resolved pursuant to the dispute resolution provisions of ARTICLE 11."
},
{
  "id": "c121",
  "name": "4.7.2 Wholesale rates",
  "text": "4.7.2 Network Operator shall provide Wholesale Service as required by MassDOT, EOPSS, ITD, and Third Party Providers at rates that are equal to or less than the Price Caps in Exhibit F, except that charges for Wholesale Services to MassDOT, EOPSS and ITD shall not exceed 85% of the applicable rates in the then-current Price Schedule."
},
{
  "id": "c122",
  "name": "4.7.3 Wholesale Customer contracts",
  "text": "4.7.3 Each Third Party Service Provider utilizing the MTC Network and each other entity whose facilities will Interconnect with the MTC Network must execute a contract with Network Operator in a form to be approved by MTC prior to the start of any Wholesale Service. The Network Operator may not materially amend or modify the approved form of contract without prior written approval of MTC, which approval shall not be unreasonably withheld. The Network Operator hereby assigns to MTC or its designee each contract with a Third Party Service Provider, other than a Third Party Service Provider whose connection is made directly on a Network Operator Network Extension, which assignment shall be effective upon termination of this Agreement. Each Third Party Service Provider contract to which the foregoing assignment applies will contain provisions acknowledging the foregoing assignment."
},
{
  "id": "c123",
  "name": "4.7.4 Marketing of Dark Fiber Leases",
  "text": "4.7.4 Marketing of Dark Fiber Leases to Dark Fiber Customers. Network Operator will serve as MTC's agent to lease dark fiber on the MTC Network to any Dark #10069598_v13 36 Fiber Customer (which may also be a Third Party Service Provider) so requesting, other than Network Operator itself, by means of an IRU."
},
{
  "id": "c124",
  "name": "4.7.4.1 Lease terms",
  "text": "4.7.4.1 Any such lease shall be (a) consistent with the then-approved Fiber Management Plan and subject to all Network Policies except to the extent exempted therefrom by MTC, (b) on standard lease terms and conditions approved in advance by MTC, and (c) at a the price of $60/mile/strand/month which constitutes the Dark Fiber Mile fee pursuant to the Pricing Schedule, as the same may be adjusted from time to time in accordance with this Agreement."
},
{
  "id": "c125",
  "name": "4.7.4.2 Compliant lease request",
  "text": "4.7.4.2 Upon receipt of a request from a Dark Fiber Customer to lease Dark Fiber in accordance with Section 4.7.4.1, Network Operator shall present the request to MTC for approval of the lease."
},
{
  "id": "c126",
  "name": "4.7.4.3 Non-standard lease request",
  "text": "4.7.4.3 Upon receipt of a request from a Dark Fiber Customer to lease Dark Fiber that does not comply with the terms set forth in Section 4.7.4.1 (i.e., one proposing deviations from standard terms, conditions and pricing), the Network Operator shall present such request to MTC together with a written explanation of each deviation, the reasons therefor and anticipated benefits and detriments thereof. Any such request must be approved by Network Operator and MTC. The Parties will develop guidelines for their mutual decision-making regarding such non-standard lease terms, with the expectation that leases to U.S. Federal government customers requesting leases of dark fiber for use in connection with national security will be accommodated, and that #10069598_v13 37 favorable consideration will be given to leases of point to point dark fiber circuits between discrete points on the MTC Network or on networks directly interconnected to the MTC Network."
},
{
  "id": "c127",
  "name": "4.7.4.4 Extension lease",
  "text": "4.7.4.4 Where the Dark Fiber Customer requests a lease of dark fiber on a Network Operator Network Extension contiguous with the dark fiber on the MTC Network and the Network Operator and Dark Fiber Customer agree to the terms of an agreement for such lease, the Network Operator shall execute a separate agreement, IRU or instrument in writing for such lease, in its own name. The Network Operator shall disclose any such lease and its terms to MTC upon request."
},
{
  "id": "c128",
  "name": "4.7.4.5 IRU payments",
  "text": "4.7.4.5 All payments received by the Network Operator on account of an IRU to a Dark Fiber Customer during the Term of this Agreement on account of a lease of dark fiber on the MTC Network shall be payable 50% to Network Operator and 50% to MTC. For avoidance of doubt, this does not include revenue from the lease of Dark Fiber on a Network Operator Network Extension. The 50% portion payable to Network Operator shall constitute Network Revenue."
},
{
  "id": "c129",
  "name": "4.7.5 Wholesale Pricing",
  "text": "4.7.5 Wholesale Pricing. The Network Operator shall establish and publish a Price Schedule setting forth charges for each and every Wholesale Service offered. Network Operator’s Price Schedule shall be subject to approval by MTC and shall be consistent with the Price Caps as set forth in Exhibit F, as amended from time to time pursuant to ARTICLE 6."
},
{
  "id": "c130",
  "name": "4.7.5.1 Publication",
  "text": "4.7.5.1 The Network Operator shall make the Price Schedule publicly available on the Network Operator's website to ensure that all Wholesale Customers have equal and contemporaneous access to the pricing contained therein."
},
{
  "id": "c131",
  "name": "4.7.5.2 Annual updates",
  "text": "4.7.5.2 To the extent requested by the Network Operator, the Price Schedules, including the Price Caps, shall be updated on an annual basis on each anniversary of the Effective Date of the Agreement subject to approval by MTC. No increase in pricing by an amount in excess of an increase in the CPI (calculated by the same methodology as described in Section 4.9.4.2 below) shall be applied or publicized unless and until MTC has approved it."
},
{
  "id": "c132",
  "name": "4.7.5.3 MTC posting right",
  "text": "4.7.5.3 MTC shall have the right, but not the obligation, to post the Price Schedule on its own website."
},
{
  "id": "c133",
  "name": "4.8 Retail Service by Network Operator Affiliates",
  "text": "4.8 Retail Service by Network Operator Affiliates. Network Operator shall not provide Retail Services. This prohibition shall not preclude a subsidiary or other Affiliate of the Network Operator from being a Third Party Service Provider, provided that any such subsidiary or Affiliate shall enter into a contract with the Network Operator on a non- discriminatory basis, on terms and conditions no more favorable than those offered to other Third Party Service Providers. In order to enforce this provision, MTC shall have the right to audit the Retail Service activities of any subsidiary or other Affiliate of the Network Operator that is a Third Party Service Provider."
},
{
  "id": "c134",
  "name": "4.9.1 Costs and Expenses",
  "text": "4.9 Financial Responsibilities and Rights of the Network Operator 4.9.1 Costs and Expenses. Beginning on the Effective Date, Network Operator will pay for all ongoing costs of operating the MTC Network and the Network Operator Network Extensions and all costs of compliance with the terms of this Agreement, including, but not limited to, salaries and benefits of the employees of Network Operator, contractor fees, rent, travel, equipment purchases, leases and maintenance contracts, expenses of marketing and sales, customer service, billing and collection, 24/7 network monitoring, maintenance, repairs, recurring pole attachment fees, recurring conduit fees, recurring IRU or right-of-way fees, software license and maintenance and support fees, premiums for surety bonds that may be required by pole owners or conduit owners, Network Operator’s taxes, taxes imposed by municipalities on property of the MTC Network, regulatory fees applicable to operation of the MTC Network, Network Operator’s insurance costs and all other operating and monitoring expenses contemplated by this Agreement, unless expressly excepted from any such requirement by MTC in writing. Other than its own expenses in offering MTC advice in accordance with this Agreement, Network Operator is not responsible for the funding of the design, engineering, installation or construction of the MTC Network, for any up-front capital costs associated with obtaining IRUs for backhaul fiber routes between Springfield, MA and Boston, MA or Ayer, MA and Boston, MA or elsewhere, or any costs associated with the design, engineering, installation, or construction of any MBI Network Extensions, except to the extent that the Network Operator proposes to and is selected by MTC to construct any such extension. MTC and Network Operator shall work cooperatively in #10069598_v13 40 their respective capacities under this Agreement to minimize the costs that may be incurred under agreements with or otherwise imposed by third parties."
},
{
  "id": "c135",
  "name": "4.9.2.1 Disclosed Exhibit I agreements",
  "text": "4.9.2 Provisions Regarding Agreements Between MTC and Others. 4.9.2.1 The Network Operator acknowledges that, prior to the Effective Date, it has been provided with copies of the executed or draft agreements listed in Exhibit I hereto, for informational purposes only."
},
{
  "id": "c136",
  "name": "4.9.2.2 Exhibit J agreements",
  "text": "4.9.2.2 The Network Operator acknowledges that, prior to the Effective Date, it has been provided with copies of the executed or draft agreements listed in Exhibit J hereto, with respect to which, when executed, Network Operator will have the responsibilities described in this Agreement."
},
{
  "id": "c137",
  "name": "4.9.2.3 Future third-party agreements",
  "text": "4.9.2.3 The Parties acknowledge that, after the Effective Date, MTC will be required to enter into agreements with third parties other than those listed in Exhibit J in order to complete construction of the MTC Network, to construct MBI Network Extensions, and for other purposes aimed at maintaining or enhancing the extent, structure, functioning and viability of the MTC Network, including but not limited to agreements to use or obtain access to the property of third parties, with respect to which, when executed, Network Operator will have the responsibilities described in this Agreement."
},
{
  "id": "c138",
  "name": "4.9.2.4 Negotiation consultation",
  "text": "4.9.2.4 In the course of negotiating the terms of any unexecuted agreements listed in Exhibit J or of the type described in Section 4.9.2.3, or agreements with other third persons the terms of which MTC wishes #10069598_v13 41 the Network Operator is to administer or with which Network Operator is to comply, MTC shall confer with Network Operator concerning the proposed terms thereof and Network Operator shall advise MTC concerning such proposed terms and alternatives thereto, shall identify in writing any proposed terms it believes materially differ from (i) those previously disclosed or (ii) those which are commercially reasonable or prevalent in the industry, and, as a precondition to exercising the right to object set forth in Section 4.9.2.5, shall provide in writing a good faith estimate of the incremental cost to Network Operator of administering or complying with the proposed contractual term as compared with the most expensive alternative contractual term recommended by Network Operator."
},
{
  "id": "c139",
  "name": "4.9.2.5 Incremental-cost credit",
  "text": "4.9.2.5 In the event that, in the course of negotiating the terms of any unexecuted agreements of the types described in Section 4.9.2.4, MTC executes an agreement containing contractual terms as to which Network Operator provided, during the course of the negotiations, a good faith estimate of incremental cost in accordance with Section 4.9.2.4, Network Operator shall be entitled take a credit against the amount of revenue sharing payments due and payable under Section 4.9.5 after the execution of such agreement for the amount of incremental cost Network Operator demonstrates it has actually incurred and paid as a result of MTC's agreeing to the contractual #10069598_v13 42 term objected to. Network Operator shall take commercially reasonable efforts to avoid or mitigate such costs. If Network Operator incurs and pays such incremental costs during a year in which no revenue sharing payment is due and payable, (a) Network Operator may carry such credit forward to one or more years in which a revenue sharing payment is next due and payable or, if none or if the amount of the revenue sharing payment is insufficient to cover such costs, may apply such credit against the price of any dark fiber it leases from MTC upon termination of this Agreement, and (b) the amount of the credit so carried forward shall accrue simple interest at the rate referenced in Section 12.4, which interest shall be taken as a further credit after all principal amounts have been credited."
},
{
  "id": "c140",
  "name": "4.9.2.6 Credit disputes",
  "text": "4.9.2.6 In the event of a dispute concerning the applicability of this Subsection and/or the amount of any credit claimed or offered hereunder, the parties shall resort to the Dispute Resolution provisions of ARTICLE 11."
},
{
  "id": "c141",
  "name": "4.9.2.7 Agency role",
  "text": "4.9.2.7 With respect to the agreements listed in Exhibit J or of the type described in Section 4.9.2.3, the Network Operator shall act as agent of MTC in its interaction and communications with any such third parties, as appropriate or as required in order to fulfill Network Operator’s obligations under this Agreement. Network Operator shall not have, and shall take no action implying that it has, authority to terminate or materially modify any provision of such an agreement or #10069598_v13 43 to waive any material rights of MTC thereunder. MTC shall take reasonable steps to notify any such third parties of Network Operator’s role and agency relationship with MTC for that purpose."
},
{
  "id": "c142",
  "name": "4.9.2.8 Delayed Commencement reductions",
  "text": "4.9.2.8 In the event the conditions described in clause (a) of the definition of the term \"Commencement Date\" have not occurred earlier than thirty (30) months after the Effective Date, on account of delay in implementing any third party contracts or a delay due or attributable to MTC or a delay in performance by any such third parties, the amount of any payments coming due under Sections 4.9.4 and 4.9.6 between the end of the thirtieth month after the Effective Date and the date the conditions in such clause (a) have occurred shall be reduced in proportion to the average shortfall (from 90%) in the percentage of CAIs that have been connected as of the end of each week during that period. Any dispute as to the amount of any such reduction shall be resolved in accordance with the dispute resolution provisions of ARTICLE 11."
},
{
  "id": "c143",
  "name": "4.9.2.9 Design standards",
  "text": "4.9.2.9 MTC agrees that the standards for design, construction and equipment for the MTC Network are critical to (a) achieving the SLAs identified in this Agreement, and (b) meeting the schedule and financial expectations of the Parties. MTC represents and agrees that it will seek advice from Network Operator regarding design decisions and take commercially reasonable steps to have the MTC Network designed and built so as to facilitate Network Operator’s achievement #10069598_v13 44 of the parameters established by this Agreement or agreed upon hereafter in performing Network Operator’s obligations."
},
{
  "id": "c144",
  "name": "4.9.3.1 Initial plan",
  "text": "4.9.3 Annual Plan Reporting 4.9.3.1 Within sixty (60) days of the Effective Date, the Network Operator shall prepare and submit to MTC an initial plan for the period from the Effective Date through the end of the calendar year in which the Effective Date occurs. The initial plan shall include a narrative outlining the principal activities and anticipated expenditures of the Network Operator for the period covered by the initial plan."
},
{
  "id": "c145",
  "name": "4.9.3.2 Annual Plan",
  "text": "4.9.3.2 Beginning with the first business day of the fourth quarter of the calendar year covered by the initial plan required hereunder, and by the beginning of each fourth calendar quarter thereafter during the Term of this Agreement, the Network Operator shall prepare and submit to MTC an Annual Plan. The Annual Plan shall include an annual plan for the succeeding calendar year and a three (3) year plan. Each plan shall specify, among other things, expected Network Revenue, all expected operating costs associated with the MTC Network, and all CAPEX Upgrades and Updates planned to be undertaken within the respective one- and three-year periods, as well as such other information and detail as may be requested by the IPT. The Network Operator will develop the priorities and schedule for CAPEX Upgrades and Updates in coordination and consultation with #10069598_v13 45 the IPT. The Annual Plan shall be subject to approval by MTC, which shall not be unreasonably withheld."
},
{
  "id": "c146",
  "name": "4.9.4 Annual Oversight Fee",
  "text": "4.9.4 Annual Oversight Fee. Network Operator shall pay an Annual Oversight Fee to MTC. This fee shall be paid annually in four (4) equal parts at the beginning of each calendar quarter, commencing with the Effective Date, at the following rates: •Year 1 - $160,000/yr ($40,000/qtr) •Year 2 - $280,000/yr ($70,000/qtr) •Year 3 - $325,000/yr ($81,250/qtr) •Year 4 - $490,000/yr ($122,500/qtr) •Year 5 - $555,000/yr ($138,750/qtr) •Year 6 - $570,000/yr ($142,500/qtr) •Year 7 - $590,000/yr ($147,500/qtr) •Year 8 - $605,000/yr ($151,250/qtr) •Year 9 - $625,000/yr ($156,250/qtr) •Year 10* - $645,000/yr ($161,250/qtr) * For each year beyond Year 10 after the Effective Date that the Agreement remains in effect, the Annual Oversight Fee shall be the Year 10 Amount increased by the CPI (see Section 4.9.4.2 below for additional detail)."
},
{
  "id": "c147",
  "name": "4.9.4.1 Proration",
  "text": "4.9.4.1 If the Effective Date is other than on the first day of a calendar quarter, the rate applicable to Year 1 shall be paid on the Effective Date and calculated ratably for the portion of the calendar quarter from the Effective Date until the end of the calendar quarter containing the Effective Date, and the rate applicable to final year of the Term shall be paid ratably for the portion of the calendar quarter from the beginning of the calendar quarter in which the Term ends until the last day of the Term."
},
{
  "id": "c148",
  "name": "4.9.4.2 CPI increase",
  "text": "4.9.4.2 For any year that the Agreement is in effect after Year 10, the Annual Oversight Fee shall be the per annum amount of (a) Annual Oversight #10069598_v13 46 Fee applicable to Year 10 multiplied by (b) 100 plus the increase in CPI from the beginning of Year 10 to the beginning of the year in question, stated as a percentage. The foregoing may be illustrated by the following example: Assume CPI for the initial measurement date at the beginning of Year 10 is 150; assume also that CPI at the beginning of Year 12 is 165. The Annual Oversight Fee multiplier for Year 12 would be 110% (100 + 10, stated as a percentage)."
},
{
  "id": "c149",
  "name": "4.9.4.3 CPI revisions",
  "text": "4.9.4.3 If CPI is converted to a different standard reference base or otherwise revised, a determination of CPI Escalation shall be made with the use of such conversion factor, formula or table as may be published by the Bureau or, if the Bureau shall not publish the same, then with the use of such conversion factor, formula or table as may be published by any nationally recognized publisher of statistical information, reasonably selected by MTC. If CPI shall cease to be published, then there shall be substituted for CPI any substitute or successor index published by the Bureau or other governmental agency, or if no such index is published, then such other index published by any nationally recognized publisher of statistical information as MTC shall reasonably select. CPI means the CPI most recently published prior to the measuring date in question."
},
{
  "id": "c150",
  "name": "4.9.5 Revenue Sharing Payment",
  "text": "4.9.5 Revenue Sharing Payment. Network Operator shall pay MTC, within 45 days after the end of each fiscal year of the Network Operator, an amount equal to the following percentages of Network Revenue attributable to that fiscal year, and such #10069598_v13 47 payments shall be incremental to the Annual Oversight Fee described in Section 4.9.4 above: 4.9.5.1 Zero Percent (0%) on first $3 million annual Network Revenue; plus 4.9.5.2 Four Percent (4%) on annual Network Revenue greater than $3 million but less than or equal to $6 million; plus 4.9.5.3 Twenty Percent (20%) on annual Network Revenue greater than $6 million."
},
{
  "id": "c151",
  "name": "4.9.6 CAPEX Upgrade and Update Fund",
  "text": "4.9.6 CAPEX Upgrade and Update Fund. Starting with the first day of the first full calendar quarter following the Commencement Date, Network Operator will pay to MTC, within thirty (30) days after the end of each calendar quarter, the greater of One Hundred Thousand Dollars ($100,000) or Five Percent (5%) of Network Revenue, for the purpose of funding a CAPEX Upgrade and Update Fund to be held by MTC. To the extent that the amounts in the Fund exceed the amounts reasonably required for the purposes of the Fund, any excess amounts may be used by MTC for any purpose related to the MTC Network that is consistent with MBI's legislatively stated mission, including without limitation funding additional extensions to the MTC Network."
},
{
  "id": "c152",
  "name": "4.9.7 Potential Decommissioning Fund",
  "text": "4.9.7 Potential Decommissioning Fund. Starting on the Effective Date, Network Operator will pay to MTC within thirty (30) days after the end of each calendar year, an amount equal to Two Percent (2%) of Network Revenue to fund the decommissioning of the MTC Network, in whole or in part, when it reaches the end of its useful life or at such other time as MTC determines decommissioning is appropriate. If MTC determines at any time in its sole discretion that the funds so collected or any portion thereof will not likely be necessary for decommissioning, then MTC may use #10069598_v13 48 such funds or portion thereof for any purpose consistent with MBI's legislatively stated mission. No such determination shall diminish or modify the Network Operator's obligation to make the payments required under this Section for the entire Term of the Agreement."
},
{
  "id": "c153",
  "name": "4.9.8 Timing of Payments",
  "text": "4.9.8 Timing of Payments to MTC. Any payments required to be paid by the Network Operator to MTC pursuant to this Agreement shall be paid quarterly unless another payment schedule is specified herein."
},
{
  "id": "c154",
  "name": "4.9.9 Network Operator Financial Reporting",
  "text": "4.9.9 Network Operator Financial Reporting. Network Operator shall furnish MTC with the following Financial Statements reflecting all Network Operator's assets, liabilities, income expenses, not limited to those related to the MTC Network: 4.9.9.1 Quarterly, within sixty (60) days after the end of each calendar quarter, an unaudited Financial Statement for the quarter just ended; 4.9.9.2 Annually, within one hundred twenty (120) days after the end of the Network Operator's fiscal year, an audited Financial Statement for the fiscal year just ended; and 4.9.9.3 Quarterly, sufficient information and analysis to establish, to MTC's reasonable satisfaction, the accuracy and completeness of payments made or owed to MTC and of any assertions by the Network Operator that the cost of any an extension qualifies it as a Network Operator Network Extension or as any other kind of Network Extension within the meaning of the definition of that term in ARTICLE 2."
},
{
  "id": "c155",
  "name": "4.9.9.4 Officer's Certificate",
  "text": "4.9.9.4 Each Financial Statement shall be accompanied by an Officer's Certificate certifying that (a) the Financial Statement has been #10069598_v13 49 prepared from Network Operator's books and records in accordance with IFRS, is true, correct and complete and fairly presents in all material respects the financial condition of Network Operator as of the dates, and for the periods, indicated thereon and (b) there has been no fraud or intentional or willful misconduct by any Person in connection with the recordation, maintenance or preparation of the Financial Statement, or any other financial documents, record or information from which such statement was derived."
},
{
  "id": "c156",
  "name": "4.10 Long Term Wholesale Customer Contracts",
  "text": "4.10 Restrictions on Long Term Wholesale Customer Contracts. The Network Operator shall not enter into a contract with a Wholesale Customer, without the prior written consent of MTC, acting reasonably, having a stated duration of more than two (2) years for which application of IFRS would call for recognition of revenue derived from the contract more than two (2) years after actual receipt thereof."
},
{
  "id": "c157",
  "name": "4.11.1 Maintenance standards",
  "text": "4.11 Maintenance Requirements, Procedures and Reporting 4.11.1 Network Operator shall maintain the MTC Network in compliance with the applicable codes and the specifications contained or incorporated, or to be contained or incorporated, in MTC's agreement with its Design-Build Contractor, reasonable wear and tear excepted, in a manner which will permit ready access to it at all times for Wholesale Customers in accordance with the terms and conditions of this Agreement and their respective SLAs and other Wholesale Customer agreements, and so as to maintain the standards for carrier class networks."
},
{
  "id": "c158",
  "name": "4.11.2 Scheduled Maintenance",
  "text": "4.11.2 Scheduled Maintenance. Network Operator shall perform appropriate Scheduled Maintenance on the physical plant of the MTC Network in accordance with all #10069598_v13 50 applicable laws, codes and regulations, the MassDOT Operating Agreement and with Network Operator’s then current preventative maintenance procedures, which shall meet or exceed standard industry practice."
},
{
  "id": "c159",
  "name": "4.11.3 Notice of Scheduled Maintenance",
  "text": "4.11.3 Notice of Scheduled Maintenance. Network Operator shall notify MTC and any affected Wholesale Customer interconnected to the MTC Network at least ten (10) days prior to any Scheduled Maintenance which will or is reasonably likely to have a material impact on service. Network Operator will normally perform Scheduled Maintenance which is reasonably expected to produce any signal discontinuity during standard maintenance windows to be established by Network Operator. If Scheduled Maintenance must occur outside such standard maintenance windows, Network Operator shall use its best efforts to coordinate between the Parties and any affected Wholesale Customer. MTC may not prevent Network Operator from performing maintenance that Network Operator deems necessary. MTC shall have the right to be present during the performance of any Scheduled Maintenance or Unscheduled Maintenance so long as this requirement does not interfere with Network Operator’s ability to perform its obligations under this Agreement. In the event that Scheduled Maintenance is canceled or delayed for whatever reason as previously notified, Network Operator shall notify MTC and any affected Wholesale Customer at Network Operator’s earliest opportunity, and will comply with the provisions of the previous sentence to reschedule any delayed activity."
},
{
  "id": "c160",
  "name": "4.11.4 Unscheduled Maintenance",
  "text": "4.11.4 Unscheduled Maintenance. Network Operator shall notify MTC and any affected Wholesale Customer interconnected to the MTC Network as soon as possible after becoming aware of the need for any Unscheduled Maintenance. Network Operator shall perform Unscheduled Maintenance, which shall consist of: #10069598_v13 51 4.11.4.1 Emergency Unscheduled Maintenance in response to an alarm identification originated by either Network Operator or MTC, notification by a Third Party Service Provider, end-user or by any other third party of any verifiable failure, interruption or impairment in the operation of the MTC Network, or upon learning of any event imminently likely to cause the failure, interruption or impairment in the operation of the MTC Network; and 4.11.4.2 Non-Emergency Unscheduled Maintenance in response to any potential service-affecting situation to prevent any failure, interruption or impairment in the operation of the MTC Network not covered by Scheduled Maintenance. Network Operator shall use its best efforts to promptly report the need for Unscheduled Maintenance to MTC in accordance with Network Operator's reasonable procedures, recognizing that in some instances such notification may not be possible until after the Unscheduled Maintenance has occurred, in which case such notification shall be given as soon as possible but no later than the start of the next business day. Network Operator will log the time of any such report, verify the problem and dispatch personnel in accordance with its SLAs and with the MassDOT Operating Agreement to take corrective action."
},
{
  "id": "c161",
  "name": "4.11.5 NOC",
  "text": "4.11.5 NOC. Network Operator shall operate and maintain a NOC staffed twenty-four (24) hours a day, seven (7) days a week by trained and qualified personnel. Network Operator’s maintenance personnel shall be available for dispatch twenty-four #10069598_v13 52 (24) hours a day, seven (7) days a week. Network Operator shall maintain a toll-free telephone number for the contacting of personnel at the NOC. Network Operator’s NOC personnel shall dispatch maintenance and repair personnel along the system to handle and repair problems detected in the MTC Network: (i) through Network Operator’s remote surveillance equipment and/or upon notification by MTC, MassDOT, ITD, EOPSS or a Third Party Service Provider; or (ii) upon credible notification by any third party or verification thereof. Network Operator shall make and maintain arrangements for a back- up location for the NOC or remote management capability in the event its usual location unexpectedly becomes unavailable or unusable, and shall inform MTC of such arrangements."
},
{
  "id": "c162",
  "name": "4.11.6 Workmanlike care",
  "text": "4.11.6 In performing its services hereunder, Network Operator shall take workmanlike care to prevent impairment to the signal continuity and performance of the MTC Network. In addition, Network Operator shall reasonably cooperate with interconnected providers in sharing information and analyzing the disturbances regarding the cable and/or fibers. In the event that any Scheduled or Unscheduled Maintenance hereunder requires a truck roll or reconfiguration involving cable, fiber, electronic equipment, or regeneration or other MTC facilities, then Network Operator shall make such personnel available as may be necessary in order to accomplish such maintenance."
},
{
  "id": "c163",
  "name": "4.11.7 Procedures manual",
  "text": "4.11.7 Network Operator shall maintain and comply with a written procedures manual, subject to MTC approval which shall not be unreasonably withheld, documenting the preventative and restorative procedures it will use to manage and monitor the MTC Network and ensure that SLAs are met."
},
{
  "id": "c164",
  "name": "4.11.8 Outage documentation",
  "text": "4.11.8 Network Operator shall obtain and maintain such information and documentation regarding outages and interruptions of service that may be required in order to present claims for insurance covering property losses and/or to recover reimbursement from persons that may be liable for such losses."
},
{
  "id": "c165",
  "name": "4.11.8.1 Property claims",
  "text": "4.11.8.1 Network Operator shall diligently prosecute and resolve, at its own expense, any claims under the property policies required under Section 10.2 and shall apply any proceeds of such claims to the repair or replacement of the damaged property, except that, in the case of a claim or series of claims arising out of a single event totaling more than $500,000, the Network Operator must obtain the prior written approval of MTC for any compromise of the amount of the claim and for any disposition of proceeds, which approval shall not be unreasonably withheld."
},
{
  "id": "c166",
  "name": "4.11.8.2 Rental loss proceeds",
  "text": "4.11.8.2 Any proceeds of claims under the rental loss coverage of such policies, net of legal fees or other extraordinary costs of recovery outside of normal claim adjustment costs, shall constitute Network Revenue."
},
{
  "id": "c167",
  "name": "4.11.8.3 Disputed proceeds",
  "text": "4.11.8.3 Any dispute regarding compromise or disposition of proceeds of claims in excess of $500,000 shall be resolved by resort to the dispute resolution procedures under ARTICLE 11. Any proceeds that are the subject of dispute shall be immediately segregated and held in trust in an interest-bearing account identified by name as a disputed funds account."
},
{
  "id": "c168",
  "name": "4.11.9 Law-enforcement reports",
  "text": "4.11.9 Network Operator shall prepare and file with applicable law enforcement agencies any reports required by law relating to incidents involving the MTC Network."
},
{
  "id": "c169",
  "name": "4.11.10 Outage response",
  "text": "4.11.10 Network Operator shall respond to any outage or other interruption of service or a failure of the MTC Network to operate in accordance with the specifications set forth in any SLA or the MassDOT Operating Agreement as quickly as possible (allowing for delays caused by circumstances beyond the reasonable control of Network Operator) in accordance with the procedures set forth herein. When restoring a cut cable in the MTC Network, Network Operator will work to restore all traffic as quickly as possible."
},
{
  "id": "c170",
  "name": "4.11.11 Maintenance subcontracting",
  "text": "4.11.11 Network Operator may subcontract any of the maintenance services hereunder; provided that Network Operator shall require the subcontractor(s) to perform in accordance with the requirements and procedures set forth herein including applicable insurance requirements. The use of any such subcontractor shall not relieve Network Operator of any of its obligations hereunder. Without limiting its obligations under this Agreement, Network Operator shall comply with all applicable tax and employment laws and regulations in engaging any subcontractor to perform such services or any portion thereof."
},
{
  "id": "c171",
  "name": "4.11.12 Testing",
  "text": "4.11.12 MTC may, upon reasonable notice but no more frequently than every five (5) years, direct Network Operator to test Segments of the MTC Network including MBI Network Extensions. MTC shall have the right, but not the obligation to be present to observe the testing. Network Operator shall provide MTC with a copy of any such test results."
},
{
  "id": "c172",
  "name": "4.12 Compliance with Network Policies",
  "text": "4.12 Compliance with Network Policies. Network Operator shall operate the MTC Network in full compliance with all Network Policies."
},
{
  "id": "c173",
  "name": "4.13.1 Performance standards",
  "text": "4.13 Performance 4.13.1 Network Operator agrees that the performance of the Services covered by this Agreement and each Wholesale Customer contract will meet or exceed the standards set forth in the SLA the Parties are in the process of completing (in accordance with Sections 4.9.2.4 and 4.9.2.5 and which, when complete, will be attached as Exhibit E), subject to the limitations and in accordance with the provisions set forth in this Agreement."
},
{
  "id": "c174",
  "name": "4.13.2 Changes to performance standards",
  "text": "4.13.2 Upon request by either Party, MTC and Network Operator will review and agree to commercially reasonable changes, modifications, deletions and replacements of and additions to the performance standards and the service levels under this Agreement, the SLA and each Wholesale Customer contract for the purposes of supporting the continuing development, and evolving priorities of MTC, Wholesale Customers and end users. The Parties agree to cooperate and deal with each other in good faith to promptly resolve on a reasonable basis in consonance with the purposes of the review process, any differences between the Parties regarding appropriate changes to, modifications of, additions to, deletions of and replacements of the performance standards and the service levels."
},
{
  "id": "c175",
  "name": "4.13.3 Measurement and monitoring",
  "text": "4.13.3 Network Operator shall implement the necessary measurement and monitoring tools and procedures required to set baseline measurements and to measure, record and report Network Operator’s performance of the Services as against KPIs, as the same may evolve and be supplemented and enhanced during the Term, and in a #10069598_v13 56 reasonable level of detail. Network Operator shall provide MTC and its designees electronic access to such records and reports as they may reasonably request."
},
{
  "id": "c176",
  "name": "4.14.1 Audit trail and access",
  "text": "4.14 Inspections and Audits 4.14.1 Network Operator shall maintain a complete audit trail of all financial and non-financial transactions resulting from or arising in connection with the Agreement. Network Operator shall provide to MTC, its auditors (including internal audit staff and external auditors), inspectors, regulators and other representatives as MTC may from time to time designate in writing, access at all reasonable times to any facility or part of a facility at which either Network Operator or any of its subcontractors is providing the Services, to Network Operator personnel, and to data and records relating to the Services for the purpose of performing audits and inspections of either Network Operator or any of its subcontractors to: 4.14.1.1 verify the accuracy of charges and invoices; 4.14.1.2 verify the integrity of the operational status of the MTC Network and examine the systems supporting that network; and 4.14.1.3 examine Network Operator’s performance of the Services."
},
{
  "id": "c177",
  "name": "4.14.2 Performance records",
  "text": "4.14.2 Network Operator shall prepare and maintain detailed records regarding its compliance with the performance standards and minimum service levels and shall permit MTC and its designees electronic access to all such records. Upon request, Network Operator shall provide MTC with information and reasonable electronic access to such records and the service performance measurement tools and procedures relating thereto."
},
{
  "id": "c178",
  "name": "4.14.3 Audit cooperation",
  "text": "4.14.3 Network Operator shall provide to MTC’s auditors, inspectors, regulators, and representatives such assistance as they require, including installing and operating audit software. Network Operator shall cooperate fully with MTC or its designees in connection with audit functions and with regard to examinations by regulatory authorities. MTC’s auditors and other representatives shall comply with Network Operator’s reasonable security requirements in connection with audit or examination. Network Operator shall maintain financial and other records for at least seven (7) years after the end of the Term."
},
{
  "id": "c179",
  "name": "4.14.4 Audit notice and correction",
  "text": "4.14.4 Such access will require twenty-four (24) hour notice to Network Operator and will be provided at reasonable hours. If any audit or examination reveals that Network Operator’s accounting for the audited period is not correct (other than amounts in dispute and the subject of active dispute resolution procedures pursuant to ARTICLE 11), Network Operator shall promptly make all remunerative payments to MTC."
},
{
  "id": "c180",
  "name": "4.14.5 Compliance changes",
  "text": "4.14.5 Network Operator agrees to make any changes and take other actions which are necessary in order to maintain compliance with laws and regulations applicable to its performance and provision of the Services and Network Policies. MTC may submit to Network Operator findings and recommendations regarding compliance by Network Operator with applicable laws and regulations which Network Operator will analyze and consider in good faith. Network Operator shall promptly respond to MTC regarding Network Operator’s evaluation and activity plan for such findings and recommendations."
},
{
  "id": "c181",
  "name": "4.15.1 Limited license",
  "text": "4.15 Resources and Facilities 4.15.1 The use by Network Operator of any MTC Network facilities as described in this Agreement (including as described in any Wholesale Customer contracts) will not #10069598_v13 58 constitute or create any lease, leasehold interest, estate for any period or other similar interest in the MTC Network, but instead, unless expressly constructed otherwise, will constitute a limited license to use the MTC Network for the periods and subject to the terms of any Wholesale Customer contract or this Agreement."
},
{
  "id": "c182",
  "name": "4.15.2 Resources",
  "text": "4.15.2 Except as otherwise provided in the Agreement, Network Operator will have the responsibility and obligation to provide and administer, manage, support, maintain and pay for all resources (including, without limitation, personnel, hardware, software, facilities, services and other items, however described) necessary or appropriate for Network Operator to provide, perform and deliver the Services as described in the Agreement."
},
{
  "id": "c183",
  "name": "4.15.3 Personnel",
  "text": "4.15.3 Network Operator will provide and have available an adequate number of trained and qualified personnel as necessary or appropriate to facilitate and ensure the timely and proper definition, provision, performance and delivery of the Services in accordance with the Agreement."
},
{
  "id": "c184",
  "name": "4.15.4 Access",
  "text": "4.15.4 MTC will provide reasonable access to any portion of the MTC Network and appurtenant infrastructure used by Network Operator to provide and perform its Services hereunder (including, without limitation, the attendant MTC Network infrastructure, rights-of-way, access points, etc.) to Network Operator’s authorized employees, agents and representatives as necessary or appropriate for the performance, delivery and use of the Services in support of network operations over the MTC Network and for the operation, maintenance, upgrade, support and use of the MTC Network."
},
{
  "id": "c185",
  "name": "4.15.5 Massachusetts office",
  "text": "4.15.5 For the Term, the Network Operator shall establish an office in the Commonwealth of Massachusetts which shall be the headquarters for the Network Operator."
},
{
  "id": "c186",
  "name": "4.16.1 Security policies",
  "text": "4.16 Security of MTC Network Infrastructure 4.16.1 MTC authorizes Network Operator all access to its facilities and premises needed to support the Services covered by this Agreement. Network Operator shall establish, subject to MTC’s reasonable approval, and comply with written policies and procedures for ensuring the security of the MTC Network in line with industry best practices, including without limitation physical security, personnel security, access control, meeting the needs of law enforcement, and monitoring to ensure compliance with the policies and procedures. Network Operator shall submit to MTC for approval policies and procedures Network Operator will follow with respect to background checks to be conducted on all personnel of the Network Operator and its subcontractors, which policies and procedures shall comply with and be no less stringent than the then-current requirements of MassDOT, ITD and EOPSS."
},
{
  "id": "c187",
  "name": "4.16.2 Security cooperation",
  "text": "4.16.2 The Parties shall cooperate in administering security procedures regarding such access by such persons as MTC and Network Operator may designate and deny such access to all other persons."
},
