  {
    "id": "c214",
    "name": "6.1.1 Integrated Planning Team",
    "text": "ARTICLE 6. INTEGRATED PLANNING TEAM & REVIEW PROCESS 6.1 Integrated Planning Team 6.1.1 The Parties shall form and participate in an IPT in accordance with the provisions of this Article 6 for the following purposes: (i) to evaluate the objectives, substance and performance of the Services, any necessary revisions to applicable Price Caps and other pricing, charges and fees, and the pricing of new and replacement services; (ii) to evaluate at least annually and recommend modifications to, and evolution of, the Services (including KPIs and Network Policies) and determine whether existing pricing should be amended to reflect modifications of the Services; (iii) to report to MTC and the Network Operator regarding each of the foregoing areas; and (iv) to resolve disputes submitted by the Parties pursuant to ARTICLE 11."
  },
  {
    "id": "c215",
    "name": "6.1.2 IPT composition",
    "text": "6.1.2 The IPT will be comprised of two representatives of each Party, representing technology and business management, and one person representing jointly EOPSS and ITD. The IPT will be chaired by a representative of MTC."
  },
  {
    "id": "c216",
    "name": "6.1.3 IPT procedures",
    "text": "6.1.3 The IPT shall establish procedures to carry out its functions and shall meet at least once a year."
  },
  {
    "id": "c217",
    "name": "6.2 Periodic Service Requirement Reviews",
    "text": "6.2 Changes to Agreement Resulting from Periodic Service Requirement Reviews. Within thirty (30) days after submission of annual recommendations by the IPT, (i) the Parties shall make a threshold determination as to whether the changes proposed by the IPT may be implemented without an amendment to the Agreement; and, (ii) if the changes are determined to result in a material change in scope, price, terms and conditions of this Agreement, then the Parties may either negotiate to amend the Agreement (including the Schedules thereto) or consider the change during any subsequent renewal. If a mutual determination is made that such changes can be implemented without the requirement of an amendment to this Agreement, their implementation nonetheless shall require the express written approval of both parties."
  },
  {
    "id": "c218",
    "name": "7.1 Ownership of Confidential Information",
    "text": "ARTICLE 7. CONFIDENTIALITY 7.1 Ownership of Confidential Information. Except as otherwise required by law, including without limitation Massachusetts General Laws Chapter 66 and Chapter 4, Section 7, Clause 26th, each of MTC and Network Operator is respectively the exclusive owner of any Confidential Information that it may furnish to the other from time to time pursuant to this Agreement, and the furnishing of such Confidential Information to, or access to such items by the other Party and/or its contractors, consultants or subcontractors will not grant any express or implied license to or interest in the other Parties and/or its contractors, consultants or subcontractors relating to such Confidential Information except as required to perform the #10069598_v13 66 Services or otherwise meet its obligations pursuant to the Agreement. Subject to the requirements of law, including without limitation Massachusetts General Laws Chapter 66 and Chapter 4, Section 7, Clause 26th, upon request by either Party at any time and from time to time and without regard to the default status of the Parties under the Agreement, the Parties and their respective contractors, consultants and subcontractors shall promptly deliver to the requesting party any and all Confidential Information."
  },
  {
    "id": "c219",
    "name": "7.2 Treatment of Confidential Information",
    "text": "7.2 Treatment of Confidential Information. Network Operator and MTC acknowledge and agree that they shall follow the policies and procedure set forth in Exhibits H-1 and H-2, attached hereto. In addition to, and not in limitation of the foregoing, Network Operator acknowledge and agree that MTC (i) is subject to the provisions of the Massachusetts Public Records Act, M.G.L. Chapter 66 (the “Records Act”), which may require MTC to make certain information, including Confidential Information, available to the public, and (ii) may be compelled to disclose information in response to subpoenas or other compulsory legal processes, court or administrative orders or similar requests or demands for disclosure of information. MTC will use reasonable efforts to notify the Network Operator in the event that MTC receives any request for disclosure of information provided to MTC pursuant to this Agreement under the Records Act, or any subpoena or other compulsory legal process, court or administrative order, or similar request or demand, all as set forth in the policy and procedure attached at Exhibit H-1."
  },
  {
    "id": "c220",
    "name": "7.3 Confidentiality compliance",
    "text": "7.3 Network Operator has read and agrees to comply with, and will cause its agents, officers, directors, employees and subcontractors to comply with, the provisions of this Article 7 and MTC's written policies concerning confidentiality, as set forth in Exhibits H-1 and H-2 hereto and as communicated by MTC's Executive Director or General Counsel to Network #10069598_v13 67 Operator from time to time. Network Operator acknowledges that during the term of this Agreement it may receive, have access to or create Confidential Information (also referred to as Sensitive Information in Exhibits H-1 and H-2) which is not generally known by the public, nor as a matter of course disseminated by MTC, published on MTC's website or disclosed by MTC pursuant to the requirements of any Governmental Authority. Network Operator agrees, for itself and for its agents, officers, directors, employees and subcontractors, as follows:"
  },
  {
    "id": "c221",
    "name": "7.3.1 Non-disclosure",
    "text": "7.3.1 not at any time, whether during or after the termination of this Agreement, to divulge, disclose or reveal to any Person any such Confidential Information, whether or not such information is produced by Network Operator's own efforts, except (A) as specifically required in connection with the fulfillment of Network Operator's obligations hereunder, or (B) as otherwise directed by the General Counsel in connection with a disclosure request under the Public Records Act, a request for discovery, subpoena, court or administrative order or other compulsory legal process, disclosure requirement or request relating to such Confidential Information;"
  },
  {
    "id": "c222",
    "name": "7.3.2 Non-use",
    "text": "7.3.2 not at any time, whether during or after the termination of this Agreement, use any Confidential Information for Network Operator's direct or indirect financial or other benefit or for the benefit of any Person related to or that is an Affiliate of with Network Operator or with whom Network Operator is now or hereafter associated, other than MTC, nor will Network Operator use or attempt to use any Confidential Information in any manner which could reasonably be expected to injure or cause loss, whether directly or indirectly, to MTC or any Applicable Third Party;"
  },
  {
    "id": "c223",
    "name": "7.3.3 Inquiries",
    "text": "7.3.3 in the event that Network Operator (or any of its agents, officers, directors employees or subcontractors) is questioned about Confidential Information by anyone #10069598_v13 68 who is not known by Network Operator to be authorized to receive or have access to such Confidential Information, or is asked to provide Confidential Information to any such Person, Network Operator agrees to promptly notify the General Counsel and respond to the inquirer in accordance with the General Counsel's instructions; and"
  },
  {
    "id": "c224",
    "name": "7.3.4 Reproduction, return, deletion and indemnity",
