ically covering any insurable indemnity obligations under Section 9.1(a), 9.1(d) or 9.1(e) of this Agreement, products/completed operations coverage, privacy breach coverage (which may be covered in a separate policy), coverage for XCU hazards, personal injury coverage, premises / operations coverage, independent contractor coverage, broad form property damage coverage, all written on an occurrence form, with not less than the following limits 10.1.3.1 $1,000,000 (one million) per occurrence; 10.1.3.2 $1,000,000 (one million) personal injury and advertising injury; and 10.1.3.3 $2,000,000 (two million) annual aggregate to apply per project and per location. 10.1.4 Umbrella Liability Insurance on an occurrence basis including policy limits of not less than $15,000,000 (fifteen million) per occurrence in excess of the limits afforded by the Automobile Liability, Commercial General Liability and Employers' #10069598_v13 79 Liability policies. Network Operator's Umbrella Liability Insurance carrier(s) may not seek contribution from primary liability policies other than Network Operator's own."
